The sewers beneath [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/index|Hallia]] are made to carry the city's waste and are not built to be defended; there are many ways in and out. A manhole in the open-air market of [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Widdershins/index|Widdershins]] drops onto a pumping floor that feeds into the sewer proper, and the [[Anti-Zorbon Taskforce|Anti-Zorbon Taskforce]] kept a hideout further along.

Past the hideout a slow underground river runs. It is an offshoot of the Fousan that either rejoins the river inside the city or runs on down into the earth, since no second river leaves Hallia. A makeshift dock beside the water was built to move beneath the city unseen, and the Party rode it downriver in a boat.

The river leaves the sewers and runs into wild, unlit caves. It widens into a circular cavern about a hundred feet across, where a narrow three-foot ledge rings a central pit and the water plunges out of sight. The cave walls are craggy. On the far side of the pit a lift is built into the rock, and a two-hundred-foot ladder climbs from its platform to a heavy iron hatch that opens back into another stretch of the sewers. The platform is a staging area still in use, stocked with hard hats that carry lamps, flashlights, nutrition bars, food and water, and marked by no organization.

Below this the lift descends for about fifteen minutes in the dark to a cavern where purple crystals on the ceiling cast a bluish glow. Two giant serpents live in the pools there. They speak, and before they would let the Party pass they wanted to know who they were and to see a permission slip.
